  "live_records": {
    "q-124168": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124168",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273134/assets/0c1a63ca9c1b4ed14808f6b3e9d9436389615c4d46cd9e963c0627027e6b6c7d.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=-v+u+2,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-v+u+2 \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment: \n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(5,4)$ and $(1,-4).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273134/assets/978c2ddf0625a4d6c872e99a95c1377abea53d402dc83b9da750f097707defef.png)",
