    "q-124151": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124151",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273134/assets/33f7326ffe8318fca915e8cc7e02a2a4c280dd9377066f1870f3bb8067b22eb0.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u+3v+2,\\,y=v-2u.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+3v+2 \\\\ v-2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,2u+3v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-5,3)$ and $(10,0).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273134/assets/e4bea3edd3fcde575e68e36e08fc4186863b12450802eb0ee37c841975983486.png)",
