    "q-124333": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124333",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2-u,\\,y=2u+v-3.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nII. $det(A)=-2$\n\nIII. The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2-u \\\\ 2u+v-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=(-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
