    "q-162179": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162179",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2=6.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|6|=6.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
